Task 3: Understanding Grafana RBAC Structure
Subtask 3.1: Explore Default Roles
Grafana comes with three default organization roles:

Admin: Full access to everything
Editor: Can view, edit, and create dashboards
Viewer: Can only view dashboards
Navigate to Configuration > Users to see current user roles.

Subtask 3.2: Understanding Permissions
Grafana permissions are organized around:

Organizations: Top-level containers
Teams: Groups of users within organizations
Folders: Containers for dashboards
Dashboards: Individual visualization panels
Data Sources: Backend data connections
Task 4: Creating Custom Roles and Permissions
Subtask 4.1: Enable RBAC Feature
First, enable the RBAC feature in Grafana configuration:

# Edit Grafana configuration
sudo nano /etc/grafana/grafana.ini
Add or modify the following in the [feature_toggles] section:

[feature_toggles]
# Enable RBAC
accesscontrol = true
Restart Grafana:

sudo systemctl restart grafana-server
