Task 8: Monitoring and Auditing Access
Subtask 8.1: Enable Audit Logging
Configure audit logging in Grafana:

# Edit Grafana configuration
sudo nano /etc/grafana/grafana.ini
Add audit logging configuration:

[log]
# Enable audit logging
mode = console file
level = info

[log.file]
# Log file location
log_rotate = true
max_lines = 1000000
max_size_shift = 28
daily_rotate = true
max_days = 7

[auditing]
# Enable auditing
enabled = true
# Log successful logins
log_dashboard_content = true
Restart Grafana:

sudo systemctl restart grafana-server
Subtask 8.2: Monitor Access Logs
Check Grafana logs for access patterns:

# View recent Grafana logs
sudo journalctl -u grafana-server -n 100

# Monitor real-time logs
sudo tail -f /var/log/grafana/grafana.log
Subtask 8.3: Create Access Monitoring Dashboard
Create a dashboard to monitor user access:

Create a new dashboard called "Access Monitoring"
Add panels to track:
